    {
      "id": "note-overview",
      "type": "text_bubble",
      "position": {
        "x": 100,
        "y": -340
      },
      "width": 400,
      "height": 410,
      "style": {
        "width": 400,
        "height": 410
      },
      "data": {
        "label": "Note",
        "title": "THERMAL MANAGEMENT & 3-WAY TCV",
        "text": "Demonstrates temperature control using a 3-way Thermostatic Control Valve (TCV) in a hydraulic oil circuit. Shows dynamic temperature-dependent fluid viscosity calculations and heat dissipation through a heat exchanger.\n\nAfter running, compare the 3-way valve outlet temperature with its setpoint and the oil temperature before and after the heat exchanger. Lines run at up to about 4.8 m/s, above the usual 2 to 3 m/s guideline for liquid lines: the pipe sizes are chosen for demonstration.\n\nInstruments: TIT 101 and FIT 102 on the oil supply to the process, FIT 103 cooler flow and PIT 104 pump discharge pressure. Solve all cases: hot oil sends more flow through the cooler, a stuck TCV or a cold start trips the temperature alarms.",
        "fontSize": "md"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "warm-reservoir",
      "type": "tank",
      "position": {
        "x": 100,
        "y": 250
      },
      "data": {
        "label": "Warm Oil Reservoir (55°C)",
        "level_m": 2.0,
        "elevation_m": 0.0,
        "temperature_k": 328.15
      }
    },
